# English comments in code

Comments inside fenced code and SQL blocks are always English.

- Prose, headings, and practice text are English.
- The first time a course term appears, its Hebrew name may follow once in parentheses.
- `//`, `/* */`, `#`, and `--` comments inside a fence are English.
- Do not mix a Hebrew explanation into a code comment. Put that explanation in the paragraph around the block.
